 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nCharacter style assignment fails when rStyle element already exists\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen setting a character style on a run that already has an rStyle element, the style assignment doesn't work correctly. The existing rStyle element should be updated with the new value, but instead a new rStyle element is being added.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom docx import Document\nfrom docx.shared import Inches\n\n# Create a document with a run that has an existing character style\ndoc = Document()\nparagraph = doc.add_paragraph()\nrun = paragraph.add_run(\"Sample text\")\n\n# Set initial style\nrun.style = \"Emphasis\"\n\n# Try to change the style - this should update the existing rStyle element\nrun.style = \"Strong\"\n\n# The run should now have the \"Strong\" style, but the behavior is incorrect\n```\n\nThe issue occurs when a run already contains an rStyle element and you try to assign a new character style. Instead of updating the existing element's value, the code incorrectly tries to add a new rStyle element.\n</issue>\n",
